      <activity id="9963e00d-8b5b-53a7-9236-12ff40e0bb8b" activityNameId="a6eb1268-d282-542c-8987-7474131406e5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Electricity, production mix MX</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Electricity, production mix MX
Electricity domestic net production shares are based on IEA statistics for the year 2008.;
UUID: 0016d799-566a-3a58-bf88-48e3a349ee00
It includes the shares of domestic electricity production by technology at the busbar. It does not include transformation, transport nor distribution losses. Photovoltaic electricity modelled with country-specific dataset that was created within project 174; Philippe Stolz, June 2020.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers in Mexico.
Technology: No technology description is provided because the dataset just describes the power plant portfolio of the respective country using current (2004) average technology per energy carrier.
Time period: Time period of statistics used (2008).
Production volume: 259 TWh
Sampling: Statistical data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0016d799-566a-3a58-bf88-48e3a349ee00.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
